From beaff74b24ed68eeb63abcf9644f047c4d3643ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Denton <z@chdenton.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:40:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] loom: avoid VMEM completion waits for interlocked GFX11 SGPR
 sources

GFX11 VMEM address/resource SGPR reads are interlocked against later
register writes. Holding these sources until VMEM load/store completion
adds false storage dependencies, delays useful work, and can invalidate
the cyclic wait frontier when the physical allocator reuses an address.

Publish this target fact for RDNA3, RDNA3.5, generic GFX11 and RDNA4m.
Keep asynchronous result-write leases, SMEM completion handling, tensor
leases and GFX12.5 XCNT source tracking intact.

LLVM enables FeatureVMEMtoScalarWriteHazard for GFX10.1, not GFX11.
Its fixVMEMtoScalarWriteHazards uses source-consumption synchronization,
not a general rule that memory completion precedes source-register reuse:
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/AMDGPU.td
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/GCNHazardRecognizer.cpp

Add a minimal gfx1151 assembly regression that reuses a load's address
SGPR immediately but waits before consuming its destination VGPR.
Update branch, allocation and spill fixtures for the shorter SGPR lifetime;
parameterize descriptor tests to cover both source-lifetime policies.

Validation against the public ecaaf7376 base plus HRX's carried fixes:
138 descriptor tests, 582 non-WASM fixture suites, 17 H3 GPU tests.
Ten alternating decoder comparisons produce byte-identical RGB and a
4.49 s candidate median versus 4.50 s with the previous compiler.
